{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2617","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2617","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2617\",\"parent_revision\":\"baef4e2a128e455d034fbb04f2a495d03dfdf05d\",\"root_revision\":\"0ec6ba5b9acf39fb9f5d0687f868d88c682a03f355e60d8b9959e733cefccea4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/monitor.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_resolver.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/dh_migrate.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/dh_config.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/linear_client.py`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Type errors in external API responses (GitHub GraphQL, Linear, config YAML) are invisible until runtime\\n- IDE/ty cannot provide type-safe access to fields \u2014 `.get(\\\"name\\\")` returns `object | None`, not `str | None`\\n- Downstream consumers must cast again, propagating weak typing through the codebase\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer maintaining this codebase**, I want to **replace cast(dict[str, Any]) and cast(dict[str, object]) patterns with TypedDict or Pydantic models** so that **type errors in external data are caught at parse time, not at runtime**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session audit 2026-06-08 \u2014 grep for cast() patterns\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-06-08\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-11)\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n| Category | Proposed Change Excerpt | Mission Source Violated | Citation |\\n|----------|------------------------|-------------------------|----------|\\n| \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-11T08:15:31.051102Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\n### Rationale\\n\\nThe proposed refactoring to replace `cast(dict[str, Any])` and `cast(dict[str, object])` patterns with TypedDict or Pydantic models is directly aligned with the development-harness product mission.\\n\\n**Mission Alignment:** The development-harness explicitly owns data structure typing and type safety as part of the process orchestration layer. Removing runtime-opaque `cast()` calls and replacing them with validated TypedDict/Pydantic models strengthens the type boundary enforcement the harness design depends on.\\n\\n**Historical Direction (Merged PRs):** The proposed change extends the pattern established in merged commit b1086e8 (2026-06-08, \\\"refactor(backlog_core): replace cast() with type-safe constructs\\\") which refactored `artifact_provider.py` and `linear_client.py` to replace `cast()` calls with `TypeGuard` narrowing and runtime validation. Prior merges 908f92c and 1f346bb followed the same pattern.\\n\\n**Legitimate Exceptions Preserved:** The item correctly identifies two exceptions that should remain \u2014 `cast(\\\"str\\\", plan)` in sam_schema/server.py and `cast(\\\"AuthenticatedUser\\\", gh.get_user())` in artifact_provider.py \u2014 both are post-validation narrowings or externally-constrained API limitations.\\n\\n**Type System Strengthening:** The proposed change directly advances the stated project principle: \\\"The type system should fail loudly (at parse time) when external data does not match expectations, not silently at field access time.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n0 concerns identified \u2014 proposed change is consistent with product mission and historical direction.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nDiscovered during session audit (2026-06-08):\\n\\n```\\nplugins/development-harness/skills/kage-bunshin/scripts/monitor.py:309,311:\\n    return cast(\\\"list[dict[str, Any]]\\\", list(data.values()))\\n    return cast(\\\"list[dict[str, Any]]\\\", data)\\n\\nplugins/development-harness/scripts/manifest_resolver.py:200:\\n    return cast(\\\"dict[str, Any]\\\", _normalize_for_json(raw))\\n\\nplugins/development-harness/scripts/dh_migrate.py:609,637:\\n    meta: dict[str, object] = cast(\\\"dict[str, object]\\\", meta_raw) if isinstance(meta_raw, dict) else {}\\n\\nplugins/development-harness/dh_config.py:89,148,155:\\n    return cast(\\\"dict[str, object]\\\", data)\\n    sub_backend = cast(\\\"dict[str, object]\\\", backend_section).get(\\\"backend\\\")\\n    global_name = cast(\\\"dict[str, object]\\\", backend_section).get(\\\"name\\\")\\n\\nplugins/development-harness/backlog_core/linear_client.py:173,179,204,210:\\n    result_d = cast(\\\"dict[str, object]\\\", result)\\n    return cast(\\\"dict[str, object]\\\", attachment)\\n    return cast(\\\"list[dict[str, object]]\\\", nodes)\\n```\\n\\nTotal: 26 instances of `Any` type and many `cast()` calls in development-harness Python files.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root Cause Design Bug\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen reading JSON/YAML/GraphQL responses from external sources, the code uses `dict[str, Any]` or `dict[str, object]` instead of defining TypedDicts or Pydantic models for the expected structure. The `cast()` call makes the type checker believe the data matches the declared type without enforcing it.\\n\\nDesign intent: external data enters the system through typed boundaries. The type system should fail loudly (at parse time) when external data does not match expectations, not silently at field access time.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`cast()` is used to narrow `Any` or `object` typed values instead of defining TypedDict or Pydantic models. This violates the project rule \\\"never accept cast over a TypedDict or Pydantic class\\\" and weakens the type system \u2014 type errors in data structure are only caught at runtime (as `KeyError` or `AttributeError`) rather than at parse time.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix Direction\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFor each cast site:\\n1. Define a TypedDict (for read-only external data shapes) or Pydantic model (for validated data)\\n2. Replace `cast()` with typed dict construction or `Model.model_validate(...)`\\n3. Let the model validate the structure at the boundary \u2014 field access becomes type-safe downstream\\n\\nLegitimate casts to keep (do NOT replace):\\n- `cast(\\\"str\\\", plan)` in `sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 post-validated narrowing after a None-guard, documented with a comment\\n- `cast(\\\"AuthenticatedUser\\\", gh.get_user())` in `artifact_provider.py` \u2014 PyGitHub returns a union type with no public discriminant\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root Cause (Design Bug)\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen reading JSON/YAML/GraphQL responses from external sources, the code uses `dict[str, Any]` or `dict[str, object]` instead of defining TypedDicts or Pydantic models for the expected structure. The `cast()` call makes the type checker believe the data matches the declared type without enforcing it.\\n\\nDesign intent: external data enters the system through typed boundaries. The type system should fail loudly (at parse time) when external data does not match expectations, not silently at field access time.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"07e9cd2303d97113eb30010e99e50a86abb1296ab527c131bc54e652086882bc\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg1m9Q\"}"}